A||||12||Shiner||Alchohol Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||12-10-1999||12:16 AM||||Is it possible to convert the 2.8 to burn alchohol?  I know it would probably wear the engine too quickly (with alchohol "cleaning" up the cylinder walls of oil), but it sure would be neat.  Has anybody ever done this?  I am not going to go out and convert my GT over to alchohol, but it's a fun idea anyway, heh.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||12-10-1999||12:40 AM||||would alcohol burn too hot to use teflon-coated cylinders?<P>actually.. do any cars (street or track) use teflon as a permanent lubricant? might be a silly question.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||12-10-1999||12:58 AM||||Intresting idea... permanent cylinder lubrication!  It would definatly wear too fast with alloy pistons and steel rings inside it though.  Maybe if you made some kind of teflon rings?  The teflon would probably heat up and break down though.  I wish car engine manufacturers took the hint, and made cylinder wall sleaves, like motorcycle builders do...||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-10-1999||01:17 AM||||I'm not familiar with the construction of motorcycle engines.. how do the cylinders differ from car engines?||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-10-1999||07:08 AM||||Don't know about newer bike engines, but the older ones had cylinders that were removeable after you took the head off. If you had a cylinder all scratched up, then you could just replace it. Very similar to the old style VW bugs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||12-10-1999||12:23 PM||||ahh.. ok, makes sense!<P>Yeah that would be a good idea for cars.. might make it possible for cars that run on hydrogen as well, as the steel cylinders could be replaced when they became brittle.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shiner||12-10-1999||12:41 PM||||I really don't know why this technology is not used in automobiles.  Time for a rebuild? Pull it apart, remove the sleaves, and bingo! No need to have the block bored over.  I would recommend that anyone with a little bit of technical knowledge go look at the design of modern motorcycle engines.  Especially some of the more exotic Honda engines (RC series).  This stuff is crazy.  Oval pistons, anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||12-10-1999||01:23 PM||||I seen couple of those hydrogen cars, england is experimenting with one.  <BR>So i guess Fiero Alcohol Funny Cars wont work?<BR>I got a bug and the engine rebuilds are only 250 bucks and you can get a complete with heads for less then 500.  Trans goes for 300.  Rust is the only thing that sucks about the car, and theres so many things you can do with the engine, and get more then 300hp out of them.||||reg||1
